WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.880 --> 00:00:03.610
In Nagoya, your app
offers Spanish and French,

2
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:05.690
and a Japanese reader gets English.

3
00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:11.410
The app's gt.config.json lists
Spanish and French, and nothing else.

4
00:00:12.320 --> 00:00:17.480
General Translation uses its AI agent
Locadex to open pull requests that

5
00:00:17.520 --> 00:00:18.710
translate your app.

6
00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:23.610
Connect GitHub in the Dashboard, and
create an automation from a template.

7
00:00:24.160 --> 00:00:29.210
Run setup with Japanese as a target,
and Locadex opens a pull request.

8
00:00:29.740 --> 00:00:35.290
Turn on auto-merge, and Locadex merges
its pull requests when checks pass.

9
00:00:35.800 --> 00:00:40.010
After the merge, the automation
translates into every target language.

10
00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:44.890
Along with Spanish and French, your
app now opens in Japanese in Nagoya.
